As I've posted before, and as a natural extension of
HJC's suggestion, all that is needed to keep pets
out of mischief in Sokoban is to carry a few pet
BUC IDed cursed items to drop places you don't want
pets to go (mainly, down the hallway with the pits,
ahead of your boulder). One such item acts to cut
down the odds against "pet between my boulder and
the pit problem" considerably, two such items in a
row cuts the odds down much farther, since even the
pet who stepped on one cursed item has much better
odds to step back onto the space with no item, than
onto the opposite space with a second cursed item.

I find a stack of cursed darts is pretty much ideal
for this purpose. They are usually encountered
early, especially by PCs who methodically untrap all
dart and arrow traps, they are light weight even in
modest bulk, and they only use one inventory slot.

Having pets in Sokoban is a real benefit if Sokoban
is a natural stop for you on the way to protection
racketeering -- they suck up all the XPs the
protection racketeer is trying to avoid, by killing
the monsters for the PC.

If the PC stays at XL:1, there is rarely anything in
the way of tough monsters in all but the most
extremely deep Sokoban entrance levels that the pets
can't handle, especially if the PC brings several
pets to Sokoban to divide received damage among them.
For those levels, running away or dust Es suffice.

Besides, it's lots more fun to do Sokoban with
out-maneuvering pets added to the challenge,
otherwise, once you've solved all the Sokoban
levels, it gets a bit boring hitting the exact same
set of motion keystrokes game after game.

